BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sean Strickland Shirt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T140000
UID:blogto-237120@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/27/original_imagec6670d0d-0968-4f31-902c-65bbc815a4
 c4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sean Strickland Shirt Becomes a Trending Favorite Among UFC Fa
 ns\nour official website https://www.bonfire.com/sean-strickland-shirt/\nT
 he Sean Strickland Shirt has become one of the latest pieces of fan mercha
 ndise gaining attention across the MMA community. As the former UFC middle
 weight champion continues to make headlines with his outspoken personality
  and unforgettable appearances\, supporters are looking for new ways to sh
 ow their appreciation\, and apparel inspired by Strickland has quickly bec
 ome a popular choice.\nKnown for his fearless fighting style and unfiltere
 d interviews\, Sean Strickland has built a loyal fan base that extends wel
 l beyond the Octagon. Whether he is preparing for a major fight\, speaking
  candidly during media events\, or sharing videos from his training sessio
 ns\, the UFC star consistently generates conversation. That growing popula
 rity has naturally led to increased demand for shirts featuring quotes\, g
 raphics\, and designs inspired by his career.\nMany of the newest Sean Str
 ickland shirts feature bold typography\, vintage fight-inspired artwork\, 
 or humorous references to some of his most memorable moments. Fans appreci
 ate designs that capture his straightforward personality while celebrating
  his accomplishments inside the cage. From minimalist prints to eye-catchi
 ng graphics\, there is a wide variety of styles available for collectors a
 nd MMA enthusiasts.\nThe recent surge in interest has also been fueled by 
 social media. Photos of Strickland wearing casual clothing during workouts
  and public appearances frequently go viral\, inspiring creative merchandi
 se from independent designers. As fans share these designs online\, the Se
 an Strickland Shirt continues to gain visibility among both longtime follo
 wers and newer UFC audiences.\nBeyond being simple fan apparel\, these shi
 rts have become a way for supporters to express their connection to one of
  mixed martial arts' most recognizable personalities. Many wear them durin
 g UFC fight nights\, training sessions\, fitness events\, or everyday acti
 vities\, making the merchandise both fashionable and meaningful for combat
  sports fans.\nAs the UFC calendar continues to feature high-profile event
 s\, interest in fighter-inspired merchandise is expected to remain strong.
  Sean Strickland's unique personality\, combined with his willingness to s
 peak his mind\, ensures that he remains one of the sport's most talked-abo
 ut figures. That attention continues to translate into demand for apparel 
 celebrating his career.\nWhether purchased as a collectible\, a gift\, or 
 everyday casual wear\, the Sean Strickland Shirt has become a standout ite
 m for MMA fans looking to represent one of the UFC's most authentic and re
 cognizable competitors.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sean-strickland-shirt-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sean Strickland trolls Dustin Poirier over arrest video in new tra
 ining photos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T140000
UID:blogto-237115@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/27/original_imageb7102ac3-a584-4759-bbdd-64317a0a5b
 ff.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sean Strickland wore a t-shirt to training that appears to sho
 w a phrase used by Dustin Poirier during his recent arrest.\nofficial Webs
 ite https://www.bonfire.com/sean-strickland-shirt/\nFormer UFC lightweight
  and BMF title contender Poirier was arrested in Georgia on Sunday night\,
  with footage emerging in the coming days. The video has gone viral\, with
  the fighter admitting later that he has been struggling with life after f
 ighting.\nAfter producing two of the greatest upsets in UFC history\, is i
 t time to give Sean Strickland his flowers?\nSean Strickland speaks on the
  mic inside the cage after his win over Khamzat Chimaev at UFC 328\nCredit
 : Ed Mulholland/Zuffa LLC via Getty Images Yeah I think this is accurate. 
 Maybe worth revisiting if he can defend the title Featured comment Feels h
 arsh to downplay Strickland's win over Chimaev. Undefeated champion who no
 body expected to lose. Does it matter how he got it done? Have your say\nS
 ign-in now for free\nPoirier’s video has been the talk of the MMA world 
 during a relatively quiet week in the sport. And middleweight champion Str
 ickland seems to have found humor in his fellow athlete’s outburst with 
 a new t-shirt he is wearing to train.\nEXCLUSIVE: Johnny Eblen claims he 
 ‘made Dillon Danis quit’ in sparring ahead of Sean Strickland’s UFC 
 title win\nSean Strickland puts quote from Dustin Poirier arrest video on 
 shirt for training\nAfter watching the video of Dustin Poirier’s arrest\
 , Sean Strickland took to social media to share his thoughts on the incide
 nt. He advocated for sobriety in a number of tweets replying to other figh
 ters giving their two cents.\nAnd he is now going viral in his own right f
 or attending a training session wearing a t-shirt that appears to refer to
  a moment in the video. Posing for a photo with a number of female fighter
 s at the UFC Performance Institute\, Strickland’s shirt reads: “It’s
  gone be bad my n—–.”During the video of his arrest\, Poirier can be
  seen threatening to fight the officer whose body cam is being used to fil
 m. He then utters the phrase\, including the controversial slur\, while sh
 aping up for a potential altercation.\nThe viral photo of Strickland was s
 hared by Veronica Hardy\, who seemed to find humor in his involvement with
  a Women’s MMA training session. “@stricklandmma just keeps extending 
 the time he has to coach Women’s MMA\,” she wrote.\nJordan Ellis\n1 ho
 ur ago\nIslam Makhachev and Justin Gaethje’s manager allegedly threw bac
 kstage punch at coach Eric Nicksick\nIslam Makhachev and Justin Gaethje’
 s manager allegedly threw backstage punch at coach Eric Nicksick\nHarvey L
 eonard\n3 hours ago\nManuel Torres reacts to UFC’s new AI rankings kicki
 ng out rival Rafael Fiziev days before UFC Baku\nManuel Torres reacts to U
 FC’s new AI rankings kicking out rival Rafael Fiziev days before UFC Bak
 u\nHarvey Leonard\n2 hours ago\n‘He looks terrible’… Clavicular bloc
 ked by unbeaten UFC star after getting her number on viral stream\nFeature
 d\n‘He looks terrible’… Clavicular blocked by unbeaten UFC star afte
 r getting her number on viral stream\nDonagh Corby\n3 days ago\nMerab Dval
 ishvili admits he is ‘heartbroken’ over Ilia Topuria’s defeat at UFC
  White House\nMerab Dvalishvili admits he is ‘heartbroken’ over Ilia T
 opuria’s defeat at UFC White House\nDonagh Corby\n11 hours ago\nPaul Ell
 iott throws a punch at Regan Upshaw after knocking him out with a head kic
 k at ONE Fight Night 44Credit:\nNFL veteran’s heavyweight son suffers br
 utal 6-second head kick KO in his MMA debut\nHarvey Leonard\nHarvey Leonar
 d\nSat 27 June 2026 11:00\nFollow us on Google Discover\nThings did not go
  to plan at ONE Fight Night 44 for the son of former NFL star Regan Upshaw
  Sr.\nONE Championship staged its latest event on Saturday at the Lumpinee
  Stadium in Bangkok\, Thailand.\nWhile Asia’s largest combat sports prom
 otion has largely moved away from MMA in recent months and years\, the spo
 rt has not been removed from the Muay Thai and kickboxing-heavy organizati
 on entirely.\nRegan Upshaw signed with ONE to make his MMA debut following
  an undefeated stint on the amateur circuit. But it is safe to say that he
  did not get off to a winning start as a professional…
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/sean-strickland-trolls-dustin-poirier-ov
 er-arrest-video-in-new-training-photos-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
