BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Childhood Journal Inspired IssaBel's New Single "Two Faced"  - Y
 ears Later\, She Finally Understood  What It Meant
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T000000
UID:blogto-236743@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/18/original_imagef4221ad4-2d66-4a19-a3cd-7dfffcadb8
 1b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO\, ON – Emerging indie pop singer-songwriter IssaBel 
 will release her new single\,"TwoFaced\," on June 30\, 2026. What began as
  a lyric from her childhood journal\, has evolved into a deeply personal r
 eflection on authenticity and\nunapologetically embracing who you are.\nLo
 ng before she stepped into a recording studio\, little IssaBel filled note
 books with song ideas and lyrics. One journal\, iconically labeled "Please
  Don't Open or I Will\nPut You In Jail\," contained a hook that would even
 tually become the foundation of "Two Faced\," that she finished writing du
 ring her teenage years.\nAt its heart\,"Two Faced" is about authenticity a
 nd the courage to show up as yourself\, even when not everyone will unders
 tand or approve. "In a world where so much feels filtered and curated\, I 
 think people are craving authenticity\,"says IssaBel.\n"People want someth
 ing real. They want to connect with people who are willing to\nbe themselv
 es\, flaws and all."\nThe song began as an observation about people who ch
 ange themselves to fit in. But during the recording process\, she realized
  she was doing something similar as an artist. While experimenting with di
 fferent versions of the track\, IssaBel found herself comparing her voice 
 and style to artists she admired such as Adelle. Then I had this moment wh
 ere I thought - “There's already an Adele. Why would I want to\nbe her w
 hen I can be me?'" After multiple recordings and revisions\, she and\nher 
 producer unexpectedly returned to the very first raw vocal take.\nRaw. Imp
 erfect. Honest.\nIn many ways\, choosing the imperfect take became the ult
 imate expression of the song's message.\nIn that moment\, the song reveale
 d a second meaning. What began as a reflection on the masks people wear be
 came a reminder for IssaBel to trust her own voice\,\ninstincts\, and iden
 tity. Raised in Brockville in Ontario's 1000 Islands region\nand now based
  in Toronto\, IssaBel has steadily built a following through her original 
 music\, live performances\, and emotionally driven songwriting. While infl
 uenced by artists including Carrie Underwood\, Selena Gomez\, and Zac Brow
 n\, she has\ndeveloped her own songwriting style rooted in honesty\, refle
 ction\, and emotional connection. "Two Faced" follows earlier releases inc
 luding "Devotion\," "Human Like Me\," and "Scream Out\,"songs written duri
 ng a formative chapter of her life that\nshe felt committed to bringing in
 to the world. For IssaBel\, releasing "Two Faced" isn't just about sharing
  a song. It's about honoring the younger version of herself who dreamed of
  becoming an artist in the first place. "The version of me who wrote that 
 lyric had big dreams\," she says."Releasing this song feels like proof tho
 se dreams were worth believing in.\nWith "Two Faced\," IssaBel encourages 
 listeners to spend less time becoming who they think they should be and mo
 re time embracing who they already are. Both a reflection on where IssaBel
  been and a glimpse of where she's headed next.\nPre-Save link for "Two Fa
 ced" below:
LOCATION:Virtual Event
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/a-childhood-journal-inspired-issabels-ne
 w-single-two-faced-years-later-she-finally-understood-what-it-meant-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
