BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Potato Potato Saves the World? at The Toronto Fringe Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T204500
UID:blogto-236408@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_image86b2b2bf-a767-4a11-845c-a00e45204c
 34.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sketch Troupe Potato Potato (Audience Choice TO Sketchfest\, W
 inners Sketch to the Death) is proud to announce their new show Potato Pot
 ato Saves the World (?) at the Toronto Fringe Festival from June 30th- Jul
 y 11th at Soulpepper’s Kevin & Roger Garland Cabaret. Potato Potato Save
 s the World (?) blends musical theatre and sketch comedy to show the best 
 (and worst) of humanity in the face of an alien invasion.\nFresh off a red
 -hot run at Montreal and Toronto Sketchfests\, Potato Potato Saves the Wor
 ld(?) is Potato Potato’s most ambitious show yet: a blend of musical the
 atre and sketch comedy combining Potato Potato’s hit sketches with new o
 riginal music. It's a 60-minute narrative tour de force that finds humour 
 in climate change\, A.I.\, Canadian politics\, and the millennial/ Gen Z e
 xperience\, as the group endeavours to defend the Earth from alien invader
 s in an intergalactic court of law. But\, as they review some of their hit
  sketches about politics and the environment\, the group is faced with the
  question- is humanity worth saving after all?\nCreated with support from 
 the Sketch Comedy Project Fund\, Potato Potato Saves the World(?) takes fu
 ll advantage of the troupe’s degrees in Musical Theatre and Devising. It
 ’s part sketch revue\, part musical theatre\, and all Potato Potato\, in
  an examination of the fate of art in a world headed toward AI. This isn't
  just a sketch show\, it's a desperate bid to save humanity. Catch the act
 ion in Potato Potato Saves the World(?).
LOCATION:Soulpepper Theatre's Kevin & Roger Garland Cabaret
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/potato-potato-saves-the-world-at-the-tor
 onto-fringe-festival-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
