BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Open Glow Studio: Self-Guided Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T210000
UID:blogto-236966@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_imagebeef0ff4-8373-450b-8012-32a8e5d648
 7f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Freestyle Glow-in-the-Dark Painting: Self-Guided Experience\nS
 tep into a glowing\, immersive art experience where creativity will litera
 lly shine. Under UV lighting\, explore bold expression using neon and glow
 -in-the-dark paints in a unique studio setting designed to inspire.\nWhat 
 to Expect\nThis self-guided session blends art and atmosphere for a visual
 ly striking\, sensory-driven experience. Inside our glow studio\, you’ll
  work with vibrant neon pigments that transform under blacklight—creatin
 g artwork that is dynamic\, expressive\, and completely your own.\nSelf-Gu
 ided Format\nEnjoy the freedom to create at your own pace. Whether you cho
 ose to freehand your design or trace a pre-selected image\, our team will 
 be available for light guidance and support as needed. Go abstract or pain
 t a glowing scene\, all you need is an open mind to tap into your creative
  side.\nArrival Window\nParticipants may arrive anytime in the first hour 
 to receive a painting introduction and light guidance from an Artbox team 
 member.\nAll Materials Included\nYour session includes access to premium n
 eon and glow-in-the-dark paints\, brushes\, and all necessary art material
 s. Aprons are provided\, but we recommend wearing white or neon tones to e
 nhance the glow experience—and clothing you don’t mind getting a littl
 e paint on.\nSnacks\, Coffee and Tea available to purchase.\nWho This Is F
 or\nThose looking for a more intimate\, creative experience. Perfect for a
 dults\, friends\, solo or couple dates.\nMust be aged 10+ to participate. 
 Guests 14+ may attend independently\; younger participants are welcome whe
 n accompanied by an adult. Guardians/kids can work individually or share a
  canvas. To help maintain a calm and enjoyable atmosphere for all guests\,
  we kindly ask that young participants remain supervised by their guardian
 s throughout the session. Guests attending with children may be asked to l
 eave if repeated disturbances occur that impact the experience of other pa
