SUMMARY:Multicultural Canada Day Celebration at Sankofa Square
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T210000
UID:blogto-236288@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_image379becb9-7800-4d4b-bf33-5056edd153
 39.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Community Folk Art Council of Toronto and Sankofa Square a
 re proud to present the Multicultural Canada Day Celebration 2026\, a vibr
 ant showcase of culture\, community\, and Canadian pride in the heart of d
 owntown Toronto.\nJoin us on July 1st from 12:00 PM to 9:00 PM for a full 
 day of live entertainment featuring multicultural groups from around the w
 orld performing on the main stage. Experience an exciting lineup of music\
 , dance\, and cultural performances that reflect Toronto's rich multicultu
 ral heritage and the many traditions that contribute to Canada's identity.
 \nThis year's celebration will also recognize Toronto's role as a host cit
 y for the FIFA World Cup\, highlighting the power of culture\, sport\, and
  community to bring people together from every corner of the globe.\nBring
  your family\, friends\, and your national flag as we celebrate Canada's 1
 59th Birthday\, Toronto's diversity\, and the shared values of inclusion\,
  respect\, and unity that define our nation.\nEvent Details\nDate: July 1\
 , 2026\nTime: 12:00 PM – 9:00 PM\nLocation: Sankofa Square\, 1 Dundas St
 reet East\, Toronto\nAdmission: Free\nJoin us for an unforgettable day of 
 cultural performances\, community celebration\, and Canadian pride as we h
 onour the many cultures that call Toronto and Canada home.\nFor more infor
 mation\, please visit: www.communityfolkartcouncil.com\nThe Community Folk
  Art Council of Toronto and Sankofa Square would like to thank Canadian He
 ritage and the City of Toronto for their generous support of this event.
LOCATION:Sankofa Square
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/multicultural-canada-day-celebration-at-
 sankofa-square-toronto/
