END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parkside Live Presents Canada Day with Ken Whiteley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T190000
UID:blogto-236385@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/10/original_image6f6edb4d-58ab-448c-a489-4ce827650b
 e7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Ken Whiteley\, Godfather of Canadian Children’s Music & Auth
 or Heather Beaumont\n5:30PM - 7:00PM\nSponsored by: Smiles Dentistry\nBrin
 g your blanket and lawnchairs for a magical evening of music in the garden
 s of Redeemer Lutheran Church. This FREE/PAY-WHAT-YOU-CAN. show supports t
 he Bloor by the Park Community Pantry.\nKen Whiteley has been deeply immer
 sed in folk\, blues\, gospel and other roots traditions for well over fift
 y years.  He has recorded 32 albums\, written over 400 songs\, appeared at
  hundreds of folk festivals all over North America\, received a Canadian F
 olk Music Award\, 7 Juno nominations\, 18 Maple Blues nominations and Life
 time Achievement Awards from the Mariposa Folk Festival and Folk Music Ont
 ario.  Ken’s recording\, Long Time Travelling\, is a unique reworking of
  old folk songs that was nominated for a Canadian Folk Music Award as Best
  Traditional Album in 2023. His performances offer people profound connect
 ion.\nJoining Mr. Whitely is author Heather Beaumont\, a Toronto author wh
 o will be giving a reading of her most recent work "When We Go Home\," a t
 ouching and warmhearted picture book that explores what it means to belong
  to two cultures.
LOCATION:Redeemer Lutheran Church
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/parkside-live-presents-canada-day-with-k
 en-whiteley-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Porch View Dances 2026 Celebrates 15 Years of Dance & Community!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T210000
UID:blogto-234902@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/11/original_imageb1d4b7b0-e284-4566-bb20-2bcfdb9894
 c4.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating its 15th anniversary\, Porch View Dances (PVD) ret
 urns to Toronto’s Seaton Village from July 1–5\, 2026\, inviting audie
 nces to experience dance like never before- outside theatres and into the 
 everyday spaces where we live\, work\, and play.\nIn PVD’s 15th year\, w
 e are looking back and looking very much forward. This year’s theme\, 
 “Perspective\,” invites audiences and artists alike to consider the ma
 ny ways we see\, experience\, and understand the world around us. Through 
 movement\, storytelling\, and shared experiences\, PVD explores how perspe
 ctive is shaped by culture\, memory\, identity\, and connection. Each perf
 ormance offers a unique lens — revealing new viewpoints\, challenging as
 sumptions\, and encouraging deeper empathy and curiosity. By bringing toge
 ther diverse artistic voices and lived experiences\, the festival celebrat
 es the richness that emerges when we open ourselves to seeing through some
 one else’s eyes.\nA pay-what-you-want event produced by Kaeja d’Dance 
 under the direction of Co-Artistic Directors Karen and Allen Kaeja\, Porch
  View Dances transforms front porches\, alleyways\, sidewalks\, and neighb
 ourhood streets into vibrant performance spaces\, celebrating real people 
 dancing in real spaces. This beloved\, one-of-a-kind outdoor festival blen
 ds professional choreographers with community participants\, creating a ma
 gical and unrepeatable fusion of art\, identity\, and neighbourhood connec
 tion.\nNow entering its milestone 15th consecutive year\, PVD continues it
 s tradition of bringing audiences together through immersive site-specific
  dance experiences that are joyful\, accessible\, and deeply rooted in com
 munity. The beloved Porch View Dances festival engages artists and partici
 pants from all over Toronto!\nFEATURED ARTISTS 2026\n● Karen Kaeja – P
 VD Founder and Artistic Director / Co-Artistic Director of Kaeja d’Dance
  / Co-Curator of PVD / Flock Landing Choreographer ● Mayumi Lashbrook 
 – Co-Curator\n● Jessie Garon\, Hanna Kiel\, and Natasha Powell – Por
 ch Choreographers ● Sharon Moore – Installation Choreographer\n● Kwa
 si Obeng-Adjei – Vignette Choreographer\n● Sophie Dow – 15th Anniver
 sary Indigenous Commission\n● Britta B & Allen Kaeja – Co-Tour Guides\
 n● Mio Sakamoto\, Katie Adams-Gossage\, Sophie Dow\, and Josh Murphy –
  Flock Landing Dancers\n● Jim Adams – Land Gratitude Address\n● Edga
 rdo Moreno – Composer\, Flock Landing\nGuided by an energetic Tour Guide
  team bringing zany humour and lighthearted fun to every step of the journ
 ey\, PVD 2026 commissions three distinct Porch Dances\, three Vignettes (h
 idden performances audiences happen upon throughout the neighbourhood)\, o
 ne immersive Installation\, and a special 15th Anniversary audience-inclus
 ive Indigenous commission. The experience culminates in the participatory 
 Flock Landing finale where audiences are invited to join in the dance.\nSe
 t throughout Seaton Village between Manning Avenue and Palmerston Avenue\,
  audiences travel from house to house\, guided by performers and welcomed 
 into intimate worlds of movement\, memory\, and storytelling. Each perform
 ance offers a unique encounter with dance in unexpected places\, making Po
 rch View Dances one of Toronto’s most distinctive and cherished cultural
  events.\n“Fifteen years ago\, Porch View Dances began with a simple ide
 a — bringing dance directly into neighbourhoods and creating meaningful 
 connections between artists\, audiences\, and community\,” says Karen Ka
 eja. “We are thrilled to celebrate this milestone with artists and audie
 nces who continue to make PVD such an extraordinary experience.”\nEVENT 
 DETAILS\nPorch View Dances 2026\nJuly 1–4\, 2026 at 7:00PM\nJuly 5\, 202
 6\, at 2:00PM (Accessible show)\nSeaton Village\, Toronto\nStarting at Por
 ch View Dances Lane\, Seaton Village (at London Street between Manning Ave
 nue and Euclid Avenue)
LOCATION:Seaton Village
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/porch-view-dances-2026-celebrates-15-yea
 rs-of-dance-community-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
