ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_imagecc5b27a3-0c96-43d4-be18-f22b2d107f
 c6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Can exes truly be friends? This striking\, profound\, and down
 right MESSY Toronto-based story explores the complexities that can be coup
 led with gay dating\, age-gap relationships\, interracial relationships\, 
 and infidelity. It explores grief and the intricacies of ‘moving on’\,
  as well as the differences between boundary setting and enabling mistreat
 ment.\n"EX-CHANGE OF WORDS" centers around Curtis\, an anxious avoidant an
 d over-thinker in his 40s\, who is grieving the loss of the love of his li
 fe\, while trying to maintain a friendship with his most recent ex-lover\,
  and has simultaneously entered a new romantic relationship as ‘the othe
 r man’.\nPremiering as part of the Toronto Fringe Festival\nProduced by 
 Goldenberg Productions in partnership with Vita Bella Entertainment and Da
 nny Sylvan Productions\nWritten by Danny Sylvan
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ex-change-of-words-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
