ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/13/original_image5d218003-edd6-46f2-9bee-6c3a561b02
 cd.jpg
DESCRIPTION:You’re invited to an exclusive preview of How To Be A Domme 
 101\, hosted by performance artist and aspiring institutional darling Pegg
 y Mitchell.\nEach night\, four women arrive ready for a private mistresscl
 ass. From TikTok tarot readings to strap-on sashaying\, Momme Domme weaves
  sonic intervention\, ritual and voyeurism into an embodied surrender to t
 he matriarchy.\nPart workshop\, part intervention\, Momme Domme is a seduc
 tive and surreal theatre performance interrogating complicity\, artistic c
 onsumption and the commodification of the feminine body.\nDone asking if w
 e’re dating the same guy? Ready to surrender to the matriarchy?\nPresent
 ed as part of the Toronto Fringe Festival.\nCOMPANY\nBlemme Fatale Product
 ions\nCREATOR\nBlemme Fatale\nMORE ABOUT THE COMPANY\nBlemme Fatale Produc
 tions co-creates live performances and supplementary schools that uncover 
 hidden histories using Pan-African oral traditions. Boundless echoes\, jus
 t like your mama’s mama’s mama knows it.\nRUNTIME\n50 minutes\nCREDITS
 \nDramaturg / Artistic Support: Me Time\nStage Manager: Annabel Pearson\nS
 et Designer: Victoria van der Meulen\nPoster Design: Kiko Keighery\nCostum
 e Designer: Sol Nolan Lee\nMarketing Manager: Cindy Dzib\nCast: Elena Bapt
 iste\nCast: Barbara Indriliunas Snow\nCast: Kimmie Croscup\nACCESS\nLevel 
 of Physical Access: Accessible\nCOVID-19 POLICY\nMasks: Optional\nFACILITI
 ES\nAir Conditioned: Yes\nWashrooms: Yes\nOutdoors: No
LOCATION:Alumnae Theatre Mainspace
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/momme-domme-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
