BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pedal & Paint: Bike Tour & Outdoor Painting Lesson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T190000
UID:blogto-236817@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image17354fdc-424a-47ac-b02d-bcafdaa71a
 49.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Hop on your bike for this guided ride full of fun facts\, foll
 owed by an en plein air (outdoor) painting lesson with a professional arti
 st.\nRide\nKick off the journey near the serene Wendigo Pond in High Park.
  From there\, enjoy a relaxed\, 13km guided ride through some of the west 
 end's most picturesque trails\, making our way toward the lakeshore and in
 to the lush Humber River valley. Along the way\, your charismatic guide wi
 ll pause the ride to share engaging\, little-known facts about the area. T
 he pace is casual\, making it an enjoyable cruise for cyclists of all back
 grounds.\nPaint\nOur cycling route culminates at a stunning\, historic loc
 ation along the Humber River\, where we will trade our handlebars for pain
 tbrushes. Set up at your easel for an en plein air (outdoor) painting sess
 ion led by a professional artist. You will receive expert\, personalized t
 ips on brush technique\, color choices\, and composition. Whether you are 
 a total novice holding a brush for the first time or an experienced artist
  looking to refine your outdoor painting skills\, you will find inspiratio
 n and guidance. At the end\, you will take home your beautiful painting.\n
 This is a bring your own bike event. Bikes are not included.\nAll painting
  materials are included (high quality paints\, canvas\, brushes\, easels) 
 as well as a small snack. Please see the event page for further FAQ's and 
 details.
LOCATION:High Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/pedal-paint-bike-tour-outdoor-painting-l
 esson-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
