BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teiku feat. Jason Stein and Jaribu Shahid
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T220000
UID:blogto-237087@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/26/original_image7b082824-88fb-4cdd-8381-9de84ed0dd
 4c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Chicago/Detroit based ensemble Teiku reframes unique and rare 
 Eastern European ancestral passover melodies in an improvised music settin
 g. The expansive possibilities of instant composition\, the ritualistic or
 igins of the melodies\, and the inspiration of jazz pioneers like Ornette 
 Coleman and Muhal Richard Abrams all contribute to the immersive world of 
 Teiku.\nThe band features bass clarinetist Jason Stein (Natural Informatio
 n Society\, Hearts and Minds)\, bassist Jaribu Shahid (Art Ensemble of Chi
 cago\, Sun Ra Arkestra\, Geri Allen)\, and founders pianist Josh Harlow (V
 incent Davis\, Wadada Leo Smith) and percussionist Jonathan Barahal (saajt
 ak\, Wadada Leo Smith\, Michael Formanek). Teiku is releasing their sophom
 ore album\, Klang\, this June on Ginkgo Records\,\n“The interplay betwee
 n instruments is masterful … Teiku is a testament to the power of music 
 to transcend time and space\, offering listeners a journey of introspectio
 n and spiritual connection.” Downbeat Magazine\n“Very fascinating mix 
 of Jewish music and jazz”\nAll About Jazz\n“Alternates wisely between 
 meditative readings of the touching\, traditional melodies\, and bold yet 
 nuanced timbral explorations … This continuous soulful dialog with the a
 ncestral traditions is invigorating and stimulating\, and always feeds the
  spirit of melody and freedom.” Salt Peanuts\, EU\n“Striking and power
 ful” Utility Fog\, Australia\nDoors 6pm / Concert 7pm\n$40adv. $50door
LOCATION:CONTXT by Trane
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/teiku-feat-jason-stein-and-jaribu-shahid
 -toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
