BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parkside Live Presents: The Linden Trio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T200000
UID:blogto-236386@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/10/original_image64a5bf77-60b3-4570-8668-b1fc2663a8
 06.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Linden Trio\nSanctuary of sounds for urban landscapes\nJul
 y 8th\, 7:00PM\nEric Kim-Fujita (violin) Sebastian Ostertag (cello)\,  Mat
 ti Pulkki (accordion)\nSponsored by: Deirdre Slowey\, Sothebys internation
 al Realty\, Canada\nBring your blanket and lawnchairs for a magical evenin
 g of music in the garden of Redeemer Lutheran Church. This FREE/PAY-WHAT-Y
 OU-CAN. show supports the Bloor by the Park Community Pantry.\nCellist Seb
 astian Ostertag\, accordionist Matti Pulkki\, and violinist Eric Kim-Fujit
 a invite you to a dynamic\, dance-inspired concert where fire and reflecti
 on meet. The program features Astor Piazzolla’s electrifying Estaciones 
 Porteña alongside the haunting stillness of Sofia Gubaidulina’s Silenzi
 o and Joni Mitchell’s Both Sides Now. Moving seamlessly between works\, 
 the evening explores tango’s pulse\, its shadows\, and its lyric heart\,
  as well as it's influences and musical offshoots. Expect virtuosic flair\
 , close-up musical conversation\, and the rare thrill of experiencing thes
 e powerful works up close and personal.\nAbout the Artists\nSebastian Oste
 rtag has performed as a soloist with the Georgian Bay and Prince George Sy
 mphony Orchestras\, Northern Orchestra British Columbia\, the Kincardine S
 ummer Music Festival Orchestra\, and on CBC Radio and Classical 96.3 FM. F
 urther performances have included the Banff Centre\, Tafelmusik Baroque Su
 mmer Institute\, Luminato Festival\, Nuit Blanche Toronto\, Symphony in th
 e Barn\, and Sweetwater Music Festival\, as well as with the Tran-Siberian
  Orchestra\, Persian Popstar Moein\, and the Eagles.  He is currently a Ce
 ntre Director at Sistema Toronto (Parkdale)\, and a member of Interro Quar
 tet.  He lives in Toronto with his wife Esther\, and their young boy Linde
 n.\nFinnish accordionist Matti Pulkki is acclaimed for his imaginative and
  creative exploration of the vast expressive potential of his instrument. 
 Currently based in Toronto\, Pulkki performs as a soloist and with ensembl
 es worldwide. His ongoing chamber music projects include the eclectic voic
 e and accordion duo Sawtooth with vocalist Sarah Albu\, the Toronto-based 
 Freesound Performance Collective\, and the internationally acclaimed class
 ical crossover ensemble Quartetto Gelato. A passionate educator and advoca
 te for his instrument\, Pulkki regularly presents lectures and workshops f
 or composers and accordionists in Europe and North America. He holds a Mas
 ter’s degree from the Sibelius Academy of the University of the Arts Hel
 sinki and a Doctor of Musical Arts degree from the University of Toronto\,
  where his academic research focused on collaborative processes between pe
 rformers and composers in contemporary accordion music.\nDr. Eric Kim-Fuji
 ta was recently awarded a doctoral degree at the University of Toronto\, s
 tudying with Timothy Ying and Annalee Patipatanakoon. He is a graduate of 
 the Master’s program in violin performance at McGill University\, and ho
 lds a Bachelor’s degree in performance from the University of Western On
 tario. Chamber music has always been a passion for Eric\, who enjoys worki
 ng and interacting with colleagues. He attended numerous chamber academies
  including the Saint Lawrence String Quartet Seminar\, McGill Internationa
 l String Quartet Academy and the Toronto Summer Music Festival. At the cur
 rent Toronto Summer Chamber Music Academy\, Eric had the pleasure of study
 ing and performing with distinguished chamber musicians such as Jonathan C
 row\, Steven Dann and Ian Brown\, as well as his long-time instructor Mark
  Fewer and the former artistic director of TSMA\, Douglas McNabney.
LOCATION:Redeemer Lutheran Church
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/parkside-live-presents-the-linden-trio-t
 oronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pub Trivia Hosted by Almost Jeopardy!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T220000
UID:blogto-236465@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/12/original_image6f010d19-f037-4313-a8da-02a235fbe7
 d9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Think you know a little bit about everything? Grab your smarte
 st friends and compete in a night of fast paced pub trivia at Hemingway’
 s.\nJoin us on Wednesday\, July 8th for a night of Pub Trivia hosted by Al
 most Jeopardy!\nFrom pop culture\, movies\, and music to sports\, history\
 , internet chaos\, and completely random facts you forgot your brain store
 d away\, this game covers a little bit of everything. Whether you are a se
 asoned trivia regular or just looking for a fun night out with friends\, t
 his is your chance to put your knowledge to the test.\nExpect quick thinki
 ng\, friendly competition\, great food and drinks\, and a packed room full
  of teams battling for bragging rights and gift cards.\nHOW IT WORKS\n3 Ro
 unds\, 10 Questions each\nRound 1: General Knowledge - anything goes!\nRou
 nd 2: Theme Round - a new theme is announced each week @AlmostJeopardy so 
 study up!\nRound 3: Almost Jeopardy?* Round - two sets of five questions i
 nspired by our favourite game show\nFinal Question - It all comes down to 
 this: bet your points on one last question. Our glorious winners will be c
 rowned smartest team in the room and you'll walk away with great prizes fr
 om Hemingway's.\n* not affiliated with the show in any way\, obviously\nTR
 IVIA DETAILS\n🕕 Doors open at 6:00 PM. Arrive early\, grab a themed dri
 nk\, and get settled in.\n❓ First question at 7:00 PM sharp. Don’t be 
 late.\n🏆 The top three teams win a Hem’s gift card valued between $50
  and $100.
LOCATION:Hemingway's
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/pub-trivia-hosted-by-almost-jeopardy-tor
 onto-5/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
