BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nick Maclean's SNAGGLE feat the ALI BROS: An Asimov-inspired Jazz-
 Funk journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T230000
UID:blogto-234482@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/01/original_imagee5d9c2d1-f59a-4524-9ba5-1bf70b40bc
 2d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Nick Maclean's SNAGGLE feat the ALI BROS: An Asimov-inspired J
 azz-Funk journey (Toronto)\nFRI-JUL-10\ndoors @ 6pm | show @ 8pm\n@ My Hou
 se | www.MyHouseInTheJunction.com\n2882 Dundas St W\, Toronto\, ON M6P 1Y8
 \n$20 adv\, $30 door\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1987926288041\n
 Facebook Event: https://www.facebook.com/events/26342980408734504\n----\n"
 Totally original... Funky as all hell... this ain’t any Kenny G oatmeal 
 for folks with no teeth."\n- Mike Greenblatt\, Classicalite (New York\, US
 A)\n----\nUnder the leadership of JUNO-nominated and 10x Global Music Awar
 d–winning jazz pianist NICK MACLEAN\, SNAGGLE feat the ALI BROS launches
  into a daring new chapter: a suite of electrifying works inspired by the 
 science fiction grandmaster ISAAC ASIMOV and his legendary FOUNDATION saga
 . Often described as “Canada’s answer to Snarky Puppy”\, the band go
 es interstellar using their fearless sound\, likened to a cross between el
 ectric-era Miles Davis and Rage Against the Machine\, to map the rise and 
 fall of galactic empires.\nFront and center are the ALI BROS\, the near-te
 lepathic horn duo of BROWNMAN ALI (Guru\, Jay-Z\, Randy Brecker) on trumpe
 t and MARCUS ALI (Matt Dusk\, Jason Wilson\, Mr Something Something) on sa
 xophone. Like Asimov’s psychohistorians\, they shape the future with eve
 ry phrase\, weaving complex probabilities into sonic reality. Joining them
  on this voyage are some of Toronto’s finest electric-jazz explorers: JA
 Y YOO on guitar\, PHIL ALBERT on bass\, and ADAM MANSFIELD on drums.\nWith
  performances swinging from Seldon–like moments of quiet\, calculated cl
 arity to cataclysmic bursts of energy worthy of a crumbling empire... Snag
 gle’s new repertoire doesn’t just pay homage to ASIMOV\, it channels t
 he spirit of his storytelling: daring\, complex\, and endlessly imaginativ
 e. For fans of Jazz\, Science Fiction\, and the BOUNDLESS possibilities th
 at emerge when the two intertwine... this is a voyage not to be missed!\n-
 ---\n:: Nick Maclean - keys/synth\n:: Brownman Ali - electric trumpet\n:: 
 Marcus Ali - tenor sax\n:: Jay Yoo - guitar\n:: Phil Albert - bass\n:: Ada
 m Mansfield - drums\n----\nWATCH Snaggle perform at the 2022 TU Jazz Festi
 val\nhttps://youtu.be/ggp8lHRB_RA?si=iu0j9NZ2hIB_7fbo\nLISTEN to Snaggle's
  uptempo burner 'THEORUM'\, from THE LONG SLOG\nhttps://youtu.be/YlHVbRgPY
 Nk?si=bq_CkJUweRj81s_Y\nLISTEN to Snaggle's twisted odyssey 'SAW'\, from T
 HE LONG SLOG\nhttps://youtu.be/ai2sYhw-SYc?si=EafC2ZIsd3RxYZP6\nLISTEN to 
 Snaggle's eclectic holiday single 'CHRISTMAS TUNE'\nhttps://youtu.be/RRf8U
 8cETZc?si=wfAZbOj3a5HPCd1l\n----\nFor more info:\nwww.NickMacleanJazz.com\
 nwww.Maclean.Browntasauras.com\nwww.Brownman.com\nwww.Browntasauras.com\n=
 ================================\nALL TOUR DATES\nThr-Jul-09 @ Henry's On 
 James\, Hamilton\nFri-Jul-10 @ My House\, Toronto\nSat-Jul-11 @ Lakefield 
 Jazz Festival\, Lakefield\nSun-Jul-12 @ The George Whiskey Lounge\, Newmar
 ket\nAll Tickets Available @ www.Maclean.Browntasauras.com
LOCATION:My House
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/nick-macleans-snaggle-feat-the-ali-bros-
 an-asimov-inspired-jazz-funk-journey-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Peter Asher: Everywhere Man
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T210000
UID:blogto-236611@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_imagee1f5e63d-13b1-4c98-933a-98f6f2bf22
 bc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Everywhere Man is a feature-length documentary inspired by mus
 ician\, producer\, and manager Peter Asher’s celebrated cabaret show A M
 usical Memoir of the ’60s and Beyond. Like his stage performance\, the f
 ilm traces an extraordinary life lived at the centre of modern music histo
 ry.\nFrom his early years as a child actor in 1950s London to the Swinging
  Sixties\, Asher emerges as a Zelig-like figure in the culture of the era:
  one half of the pop duo “Peter and Gordon\,” recipients of four chart
 -topping hits penned by Paul McCartney\; the first head of A&R at Apple Re
 cords\; and co-owner of the Indica Gallery\, the epicenter of London’s c
 ountercultural art scene.\nAsher helped define a generation of singer-song
 writers as producer and manager for James Taylor\, Linda Ronstadt\, and ot
 hers\, cementing his reputation as one of music’s most influential behin
 d-the-scenes forces of the 1970s and ‘80s. In the present day\, he remai
 ns a vital creative force\, still performing\, producing\, and most recent
 ly collaborating with Barbra Streisand on her acclaimed The Secret of Life
  duets album.\nFeaturing intimate interviews with James Taylor\, Linda Ron
 stadt\, Carole King\, Kate Taylor\, Lyle Lovett\, Natalie Merchant\, Maria
 nne Faithfull\, Paul Jones\, Danny Kortchmar\, Waddy Wachtell\, Lee Sklar\
 , John Boylan\, Paul Shaffer\, and Paul McCartney [in voiceover]\, as well
  as cultural icons Steve Martin\, Eric Idle\, Twiggy\, and Pattie Boyd. Ev
 erywhere Man paints a vibrant portrait of a man whose life intersects with
  some of the greatest artists and moments of the last six decades.\nAnd th
 e soundtrack\, woven from the timeless hits of those featured\, creates a 
 score as unforgettable as the story.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/peter-asher-everywhere-man-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
