 40.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Time moves differently when you are far from home. For interna
 tional students\, the past holds memories we return to with longing and re
 flection\, the present is filled with questions of belonging and adequacy\
 , and the future remains uncertain and unfolding. This exhibition explores
  how international students carry multiple timelines within a single life\
 , moving between nostalgia\, the present moment\, and future possibilities
 .\nLocation: The Great Hall\, Main Campus\, 100 McCaul Street\, Toronto\nE
 xhibition Dates: July 16 to July 22\, 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.\, and July 23\, 9 a
 .m. to 12 p.m.\nFree admission\, open to all ages\nInteractive activities 
 (daily except Saturday July 18 and Sunday July 19): 10 a.m. to 11 a.m. and
  2 p.m. to 3 p.m.\n• Clock DIY\n• Caricatures\n• Time documentation 
 activity: I have traveled this time\n• Mandala drawing\n12 p.m. to 1 p.m
 .: Artist Talk
LOCATION:The Great Hall\, OCAD University
