BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Small Movements: A Performance by Adam Basanta
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T200000
UID:blogto-237053@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/25/original_image9d247cd9-1478-4156-af33-e05c6d1abd
 5e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at MOCA for an intimate sound performance by multimedi
 a artist Adam Basanta.\nUsing tuned microphone feedback\, modified amplifi
 cation techniques\, and kinetic elements\, Basanta creates delicate sonic 
 compositions with handheld microphones\, speakers\, cassette recorders\, c
 ustom software\, and everyday objects.\nThis performance is presented with
 in Sara Cwynar’s exhibition Baby Blue Benzo Beta. While Cwynar’s work 
 examines how images\, technology\, and systems of value shape our desires 
 and understanding of the world\, Basanta turns our attention to the hidden
  mechanics of sound production and perception.\nThe performance will be pr
 esented twice\, at 6 pm and 7:30 pm.
LOCATION:MOCA Toronto
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/small-movements-a-performance-by-adam-ba
 santa-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music: Improbable Places
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260717T213000
