BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dakshin Diaries of South India with Kasturi & Deepthy of BiteBox
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T210000
UID:blogto-234324@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/28/original_image5a71f2f6-e4c5-4861-b329-9e1b58fc6d
 98.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Dakshin Diaries is a curated BiteBox experience from Tales & T
 iffin Supper Club that takes guests on a journey across South India in the
  form of a multi-course extravaganza of creative small plates that both ho
 nor classic roots and playfully incorporate contemporary elements.\nEach d
 ish represents a different region of South India\, reimagined into elegant
 \, bite-sized formats that balance authenticity with modern presentation. 
 Rooted in storytelling and thoughtful curation\, this story of South India
  brings together diverse flavors\, textures\, and traditions into a seamle
 ss\, immersive tasting experience.\nMENU\nKal Dosa Canapé with Mushroom C
 hukka & Curry Leaf Oil (Tamil Nadu)\nSoft mini kal dosa (a thicker\, softe
 r\, and spongier variant of a plain dosa with crisp edges) topped with pep
 pery mushroom and fennel chukka (a dry-roasted curry) with curry leaves 
 — earthy\, bold\, and deeply comforting.\nMalabar Vegetable Tartlet with
  Coconut Cream (Kerala)\nA delicate tart filled with coconut-laced carrots
 \, green beans\, potatoes and peas. Mild\, aromatic\, and beautifully bala
 nced. Inspired by Kerala's famous vegetable stews.\nMini Mangalore Bun Sli
 ders with Coconut Chutney (Karnataka)\nLight\, fluffy buns with a hint of 
 sweetness and notes of banana\, paired with a savory chutney made from coc
 onut\, green chiles and a blend of spices.\nKaaram Poli Coins with Green C
 hile & Coconut Filling (Andhra Pradesh)\nSoft poli discs (unique flatbread
 s related to paratha\, but softer and more delicate) layered with a fiery 
 green chile chana dhal (chick pea curry) and coconut filling. Kaaram refer
 s to a higher spice/heat level typical of Andhra Pradesh. Bold\, vibrant\,
  and unexpected.\nShikampuri Kebab Bites with Mint Chutney (Telangana)\nGo
 lden kebabs with a creamy center. Shikampuri refers to a style of stuffed 
 kabob with a rich filling. In this vegetarian version\, chana dhal (chick 
 pea curry) and paneer take centre stage while a light\, yogurt sauce compl
 etes the signature creamy contrast to the outer crisp layers. Rich\, indul
 gent\, and deeply satisfying.\nMini Orange Rolls with Citrus Glaze (Pondic
 herry)\nSoft\, fragrant yeast-based rolls (not unlike brioche) infused wit
 h orange zest and finished with a light citrus glaze. A bright\, refreshin
 g end to the meal with a French touch that honor's that country's love of 
 pairing enriched dough with a delicate glaze.\n----\nTales & Tiffin is a c
 urated supper club experience that brings together food\, storytelling\, a
 nd culture in an intimate\, thoughtfully designed setting. Each event is b
 uilt around a unique theme\, blending regional flavors\, personal narrativ
 es\, and immersive dining to create moments that go beyond just a meal. Ho
 sted by Kasturi Vishal and Deepthy Suresh\, Tales & Tiffin is rooted in th
 e idea of connection where guests don’t just dine\, but experience\, eng
 age\, and remember.\nBiteBox is an extension of this philosophy and a mode
 rn\, curated approach to Indian hosting. It reimagines traditional dishes 
 into elegant\, bite-sized portions that are beautifully presented\, easy t
 o serve\, and designed for social gatherings. Each BiteBox menu is crafted
  with intention\, balancing flavor\, texture\, and storytelling\, allowing
  guests to explore a diverse range of dishes in a seamless\, elevated form
 at.\n*Note: The menu is entirely Vegetarian except for eggs in the dessert
  course.
LOCATION:The Depanneur
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dakshin-diaries-of-south-india-with-kast
 uri-deepthy-of-bitebox-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edible & Medicinal Plants of Ontario with Stephan Lukacic in Toron
 to's High Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T160000
UID:blogto-237024@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/25/original_imagecca95b6e-9ed2-4c09-8c58-ea858e8162
 c9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Take an introductory peek into nature’s pantry and pharmacy 
 with popular outdoor educator and avid forager Stephan Lukacic.\nThis fasc
 inating workshop is focused on plant anatomy and identification skills\, a
 nd the sustainable harvest of common wild plants for food and medicine.\nE
 xploring wild plant ecology\, traditional uses\, and the modern science be
 hind it all\, this comprehensive class will not only teach you how to iden
 tify wild plants safely and accurately\, but Steve will share some of his 
 favorite ways of using them\, including delicious recipes and tried-and-tr
 ue home remedies.\nThe list of plants covered in this workshop includes na
 tive\, naturalized\, and invasive species that have both culinary and heal
 ing properties\, many of which can be found right in your own backyard. Yo
 u will receive an 8-page handout covering all the basics of plant identifi
 cation and ethical foraging\, and read and discuss its contents thoroughly
 . Then you’ll do a deep dive right onto the trails in High Park — putt
 ing the knowledge you’ve acquired directly into practice by observing an
 d identifying wild plants the group encounters in their natural habitat.\n
 Come learn everything you ever wanted to know about wild plants and a whol
 e lot more… There’s always time for questions and conversation\, cool 
 people and a bunch of laughs!\nNote: You will not be foraging for wild pla
 nts to take home. This workshop focuses on teaching you how to find and id
 entify wild edible and medicinal plants.\nPrice: $73\nAges: 18+ years\nMee
 ting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive\nPlease 
 bring:\nA pen or pencil\nA notebook\nWeather-appropriate clothing\nCuriosi
 ty\nReadiness for outdoor learning
LOCATION:High Park Nature Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/edible-medicinal-plants-of-ontario-with-
 stephan-lukacic-in-torontos-high-park-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
