 53.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The cultures\, stories and songs of Indigenous People will be 
 shared at Indigenous Sounds Now\, curated by Elaine Bomberry. Guiding this
  musical journey is Host Donna Sound\, who is a reporter for CTV’s Natio
 nal News ‘Indigenous Circle’. The incredible range of vibrations go fr
 om the heart felt beats of the Eagleheart Singers & Drummers\, a tradition
 al Pow Wow drum\, DJ’s Classic-Roots and DJ Kimivn who blend Electronica
  fusion with Indig rhythms. The Healers bring some of their good ole’ Si
 x Nations soulful blues. Nadjiwan also hits the stage with powerful lyrics
  and real slick alt-rock grooves.
LOCATION:Trillium Park
