 61.jpg
DESCRIPTION:High Park is lucky enough to be a home to many incredible spec
 ies of moths! As most moths are nocturnal\, this event will take place in 
 the evening to maximize viewing opportunities. We will begin with a moth t
 alk and then have time to observe some of the moths of High Park on specia
 lly lit sheets. Throughout the event\, caterpillar walks — searching for
  caterpillars that fluoresce under UV light — will be led by members of 
 the High Park Caterpillar Survey.  Members of the Toronto Entomologists’
  Association will be on hand to share their knowledge.\nNote: No moth coll
 ecting will be allowed.\nPlease bring:\nA pair of clear UV safety glasses 
 if you have them. The lights used to attract the moths are very strong.\nO
 ptional Items To Bring:\nA flashlight or headlamp\nA reusable water bottle
  (may be refilled at the Nature Centre)\nNut-free snacks\nMoth field guide
 s if you have your own\nA hand lens if you have one\nPrice: Pay What You C
 an ($0\, $5\, $8\, $10)\nMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 C
 olborne Lodge Drive
LOCATION:High Park Nature Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/moth-night-in-torontos-high-park-toronto
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
