 2e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A massive outdoor symphony is set to transform Toronto’s wat
 erfront this summer as Mandle Philharmonic brings Mahler’s epic “Resur
 rection” Symphony to the RBC Amphitheatre. (You may know the symphony al
 ready\, as it’s featured in the 2023 Leonard Bernstein biopic Maestro\, 
 starring and directed by Bradley Cooper.) Featuring more than 200 performe
 rs—full orchestra\, chorus and soloists—the open-air concert aims to b
 reak down barriers to classical music with a powerful\, goosebump-inducing
  experience under the night sky.\nEvent Details:\nThe Sound of Resurrectio
 n Under the Stars\nRBC Amphitheatre\nFriday July 24\, 2026\n7:30 p.m.\nPer
 formers:\nMandle Philharmonic\nMandlePhil Choir\n200+ professional musicia
 ns and singers\nMandle Cheung\, conductor\nLesley Bouza\, soprano\nAlex He
 therington\, mezzo-soprano\nFor media inquiries\, interviews or press tick
 ets\, please contact:\nJacqueline Au-Young\njacqueline.auyoung@mandlephil.
 com\nTickets: MandlePhil.com
LOCATION:RBC Amphitheatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-sound-of-resurrection-under-the-star
 s-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
