ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_imaged71a0009-d03e-4d39-bc54-e36f44fe68
 1b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Become a ghost sign hunter!\nLearn how to spot the fading pain
 ted ads that linger on Toronto’s streets—remnants of early Canadian ma
 rketing that used imagery\, typography\, and emotion to shape a national i
 dentity. Discover what these disappearing signs can tell us about Toronto
 ’s past\, and sharpen your eye for the hidden history still visible abov
 e our streets.\nThis tour will be led by Stephen Petar\, an award-winning 
 publicist and Heritage Toronto Award-winning writer. His passion for ghost
  signs started at a Doors Open Toronto event in the early 2010s. Since the
 n\, he has documented these signs worldwide on his Instagram @GhostsOfCana
 da from Canada to Greece\, France\, Sweden and more. A born-and-raised Tor
 ontonian\, he is passionate about the city’s heritage and architecture.
LOCATION:Sorauren Park Town Square
