ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_image020df84d-95c9-4b8c-b146-cb8d778748
 67.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A special screening bringing together two classic Canadian doc
 umentaries—both from 1959 and directed by Roman Kroitor and Wolf Koenig 
 who were well know for their pioneering use of cinema vérité—that show
  different sides of legendary Canadian pianist\, Glenn Gould:\nGlenn Gould
 : On the Record follows Gould to New York City. There\, we see the renowne
 d concert pianist kidding the cab driver\, bantering with sound engineers 
 at Columbia Records\, and then\, alone with the piano\, fastidiously recor
 ding Bach's Italian Concerto.\nIn Glenn Gould: Off the Record\, Gould enjo
 ys a respite at his lakeside cottage. This is an aspect of Gould previousl
 y known only to the collie pacing beside him through the woods\, the fishe
 rmen resting their oars to hear his piano\, and fellow musicians like Fran
 z Kraemer\, with whom Gould talks of composition.\nThe features will be pr
 eceded by MADE | NOUS: Stories That MADE Us episode 1:\nCross-Canada Road 
 Trip with George Stroumboulopoulos (D: Alex Craig | Canada | 19 min)\nGeor
 ge Stroumboulopoulos travels through British Columbia and Alberta\, explor
 ing iconic Canadian stories from The Beachcombers to Kim’s Convenience. 
 As Tantoo Cardinal says: “Canada\, we got stuff!”
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/glenn-gould-on-and-off-the-record-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
