DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T210000
UID:blogto-236902@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/23/original_image5ef0b768-0b61-4ec9-b416-bddaf1e6d7
 2e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:The Blues is the sound of cultural resilience\, and while the 
 genre is the foundation for modern music\, the stories of the women who sh
 aped it are often unseen and unheard.\n\nSister Rosetta Tharpe\, Ma Rainey
 \, and Bessie Smith lived exciting\, courageous\, and wild lives\, all whi
 le quietly shaping American culture through music and more.\n\nMa Rainey i
 s now known as The Mother of Blues\, Sister Rosetta as The Godmother of Ro
 ck & Roll\, and Bessie Smith as\, The Empress Of Blues.\n\nJoin creator an
 d star Divine Brown (Billie\, Sarah and Ella: Revolutionary Women in Jazz)
  and an all-star team of performers and musicians as they bring us the sto
 ry of these three extraordinary and revolutionary women.
LOCATION:Soulpepper Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/revolutionary-women-in-blues-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
