 gto.com/events/2026/06/04/original_image3ef98bff-0078-4249-b381-ee9ef9db7b
 01.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Contour explores growth\, change\, and renewal through layered
  textures\, shifting landscapes\, and expressive abstract forms.\nFEATURIN
 G ARTIST: Yangyang Pan\, Annette Mcarthur\, Divyani Chandorkar\, Steve Wil
 son\, Irina Laskin\, Daria Gavrilina\, Lynden Cowan & Joanne Lomas.\nStep 
 into an immersive visual experience where texture becomes story and time u
 nfolds in cycles. Contour is a compelling exhibition of abstract and lands
 cape works that explores growth\, change\, and renewal through layered for
 ms and expressive techniques. From shifting horizons to textured surfaces 
 that echo seasons passing\, each piece reflects the rhythms of life—invi
 ting viewers to pause\, reflect\, and connect with the ever-evolving natur
 e of memory\, place\, and transformation.
LOCATION:Twist Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/contour-opening-reception-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curators Talk: Unearthing Vindolanda
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
UID:blogto-236934@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_imagea41a2fdd-04e7-4dd7-bd78-a91d90ebdb
 fb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Date: Thursday\, September 17\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 pm – 8:00 p
 m\nLocation: Bata Shoe Museum\, 327 Bloor St. W.\nTickets: $25\nJoin us fo
 r a fascinating evening with archaeologist Elizabeth Greene\, whose extens
 ive research at Vindolanda has helped reshape our understanding of life on
  the edge of the Roman Empire.\nDrawing on her firsthand excavation experi
 ence\, Greene will take us behind the scenes of the dig: what it feels lik
 e to carefully unearth history layer by layer\, the challenges of working 
 in the soil of northern England\, and the thrill of discovering objects th
 at have not been touched in nearly two millennia.\nLocated just south of H
 adrian’s Wall\, Vindolanda is one of Britain’s most extraordinary Roma
 n sites\, famed for its remarkably preserved artifacts—including leather
  shoes\, writing tablets\, and everyday objects that offer intimate glimps
 es into ancient lives. Whether you’re passionate about archaeology\, Rom
 an history\, or the stories hidden beneath our feet\, this is an evening n
 ot to be missed
LOCATION:Bata Shoe Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/curators-talk-unearthing-vindolanda-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
