BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BORNS with Two Feet & The Blue Stones - Live At The Bowl
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T230000
UID:blogto-233782@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_image412859e6-9d71-44ca-945f-7d7a2232b4
 fa.jpg
DESCRIPTION:BØRNS\nINDIE88 GRAND SLAM CONCERT SERIES\nWITH SPECIAL GUESTS
  TWO FEET & THE BLUE STONES\nFRIDAY SEPTEMBER 25\, 2026\nABOUT BØRNS\nBØ
 RNS creates from instinct\, not expectation. A natural-born performer with
  a voice that feels both celestial and grounded\, he first captivated list
 eners with Dopamine - his gold-certified debut album featuring the viral a
 nthems “ElectricLove” and “Past Lives.” A decade later\, the songs
  haven’t aged—they’ve deepened\, mirroring the evolution of an artis
 t more attuned than ever to his inner world. In recent years\, BØRNS has 
 explored new corners of his sound with the independently released EPs Sudd
 enly and Honeybee—intimate\, organic\, and sonically expansive bodies of
  work that reflect a more personal relationship with music itself. Far fro
 m a departure\, they were a continuation—expressions of the same creativ
 e curiosity that’s always driven him. Music made without compromise\, le
 d by feeling rather than formula. Now\, with the announcement of a fall na
 tionwide tour to celebrate the 10-year anniversary of Dopamine\, BØRNS is
  reigniting his passion for live performance—and may offer glimpses of w
 hat’s next. Unconcerned with genre or trend\, whatever the future holds 
 won’t be a pivot\, but another facet of an artist following his joy. Thi
 s is a new era of freedom. Fully independent and artist-led\, every move i
 s intentional—serving the artist first\, and the art that follows.\nABOU
 T TWO FEET\nFor most of Two Feet's career\, he has bristled against the co
 nstraints of traditional pop songwriting\, the critic-approved respectabil
 ity of the album format and the handed-down expectations of what a song sh
 ould sound like. His bluesy\, bass-heavy first single “Go Fuck Yourself
 ” has no bridge and no hook\, but has earned almost half a billion strea
 ms to date. Pink (2020) does away with the chorus on many of its songs. Ma
 x Maco Is Dead Right? (2021) is a voyeuristic concept album based around a
  troubled fictional character and Shape & Form (2022) is an album he descr
 ibes as an “eclectic mess.” In 2023\, he launched an independent label
  477 Records to sign and collaborate with up and coming artists across the
  globe.\nABOUT THE BLUE STONES\nThe Blue Stones - vocalist and guitarist T
 arek Jafar and drummer Justin Tessier - formed during their university day
 s and inspired by the freedom of creating without boundaries\, grew from p
 laying small-town bars to headlining iconic venues like The Troubadour in 
 Los Angeles\, Electric Ballroom in London\, and The Danforth Music Hall in
  Toronto. Along the way\, they’ve racked up over 300 million streams\, f
 our JUNO nominations\, and radio hits like Shakin’ Off the Rust\, which 
 topped Rock charts in Canada and hit #5 on U.S. Mainstream Rock.
LOCATION:The Bowl at Sobeys Stadium
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/borns-with-two-feet-the-blue-stones-live
 -at-the-bowl-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Etobicoke Ribfest 2026
